\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{The curve determined by a velocity}
\date{2026-11-25}

\p{At #{I_{\mathrm{app}}=60} the equations of \ref{fnip-0005} assign
a velocity to each pair #{(V,n)}. A differentiable curve in the plane
has its own velocity at each time. The curve follows the equations
when the two velocities agree. How is that curve named from an
initial pair, and on what time interval does it exist?}
